      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That profound exhaustion you feel is the weight of carrying unbearable loss; it is agonizing to feel everything crumbling around you. While the darkness feels absolute, please hold on to the fact that this crushing sensation is a symptom of trauma, not necessarily the permanent truth of your future. There are ways to carry this weight that do not involve surrendering entirely, and reaching out, even just a little, is how you start to find a path through the rubble.",
      "source": "target",
