      "content": "The silence you describe is terrifying because it lacks the narrative of a fight, making finality seem like the only logical conclusion. However, holding on isn't always about fighting; it can sometimes be about radically redefining what \"survival\" means for yourself. Peace doesn't always look like a triumphant return to the old world; sometimes it is the small, defiant act of choosing to experience something, even a quiet moment, within the ashes. Your worth is not tied to the grandeur of the citadel, but to your enduring capacity to seek meaning.",
